And another good one dead.  I'd hoped this one might make it to the
quest, finally…  At least it leaves a more interesting message in the
scores file.

Two levels fairly uneventful, the RNG's food supply just enough to keep
me alive.  Found a cloak of displacement on the floor in dl3, which
helped both in keeping me alive and in entering shops.  Two large
general stores on dl4 and dl5 solved the food problem for good and got
me some more AC.  Price-ID'd my inventory and the shops' contents.  A
brief detour to the first mines level brought me to AC -5.

Removed the iron ball on dl6 and left it there to gain carrying capacity
(quite probably an error), switching to pick-axe which I had at basic
then.  Prayer took care of a cursed towel, no problem with it at that point.

I then went back to the mines hoping for a mattock; cleared the first
level and the area around the upstairs on the second one.  Became a bit
careless at this point and stepped onto a hole.  It promptly brought me
down to minetown, in one of the little rooms to the right of the main
square.

At that point I realized I had a major problem, with all the guards
hostile.  I was in full health and good enough AC, but lacking a really
powerful weapon.  The two rooms on the right were (yet) empty of guards,
but it turned out that the upstairs was on the other side.  One of the
guards nailed me down.  I managed to kill him, leaving me severely
wounded, but the way relatively clear.

At that point I ran for it and saw that one of the guards had an attack
wand that would probably mean my end – yet around a corner, but I had to
run in a long, straight line to the other side of the level, and didn't
know if I really had all guards in my back.  Checked my inventory again,
looking at the chances.  I decided that a 200zm potion might be my best
chance – an 8% chance for full healing, 67% for speed or levitation,
both of which might have helped my escape.  Enlightenment (16%) wouldn't
have harmed me either.  Of course, it turned out to be polymorph (8%),
turning me into a giant eel…  The watch captain quickly finished me off.

Back to the start.

